  {
    "sha": "b9564952f5774b986f36f9ab10761b68348f3665",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVouz_toAKGI5NTY0OTUyZjU3NzRiOTg2ZjM2ZjlhYjEwNzYxYjY4MzQ4ZjM2NjU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T07:51:34Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T07:51:34Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): machine check reads a 4th-axis table's pose through the tool axis\n\nOn a machine whose only rotary turns about X (the 770MX + microARC 4),\nthe pose check judged the canonical letters one by one and refused the\nface underneath, A0 B180, as \"states no B axis\" - although that table\nreaches it as A180 and the PathPilot post (#785) already posts it so.\n\nThe pose gate moves to machine/judge.rs (pose_problems). On a machine\nwith exactly one rotary, stated along X, it reads the tool angle about X\nfrom the letters with the post's own formula and tolerances\n(tormach.cps toolAngle), signs it by the stated direction and judges it\nagainst the travel. A pose with an X component (any B or C a turn about\nX cannot make) is refused by name. Every other machine keeps the letter\nlaw unchanged.\n\nfanuc.cps writes the stream's letters as they come, so it now refuses a\nturning letter with no rotary of that name. The A0 B180 the check now\npasses on an A-only table can never reach that control as a B word.\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/fourth_axis_pose.rs; the microARC wrap test\nnow expects the post's refusal (simultaneous 4-axis) instead of the\ncheck's B180 one.\n\nFixes #797\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
