  {
    "sha": "d1c73221a2ee2132df39fddd4573463a122caacb",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVouz_toAKGQxYzczMjIxYTJlZTIxMzJkZjM5ZmRkZDQ1NzM0NjNhMTIyY2FhY2I",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T17:00:02Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T17:00:02Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): fanuc refuses a lone A stated along -X; reword the pose doc\n\nPR #803 review: the machine check judges a lone rotary about X by the\nnegated angle on a [-1,0,0] table, but fanuc.cps writes the stream's A\nunnegated, so a pose the check passed could post outside the judged\ntravel. The Fanuc dialect now refuses that tilt by name. judge.rs no\nlonger claims every post agrees with the check: only the PathPilot\npost does; Fanuc refuses the B of A0 B180 and the -X table.\n\nPinned by fourth_axis_pose::the_fanuc_dialect_refuses_a_lone_a_stated_along_minus_x.\n\nRefs #797\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
