  {
    "sha": "693b2809d7220d7616a917eb9a359259dfeec53f",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVouz_toAKDY5M2IyODA5ZDcyMjBkNzYxNmE5MTdlYjlhMzU5MjU5ZGZlZWM1M2Y",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T19:17:21Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T19:17:21Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): doosan refuses a missing letter and a turning -X A; fanuc keeps A0\n\nPR #803 delta review: doosan-dnm.cps's RTCP path (the shipped DNM's\nA about X leans off Z, so machine.rtcp is set) wrote the stream's\nletters raw. With the machine check now passing A0 B180 on an A-only\ntable, it would have posted a B180 word to a machine with no B, and a\nturning A unnegated on a [-1,0,0] table. It now refuses both by name,\nas fanuc.cps does. Both posts refuse only a non-zero A on the -X\ntable: A0 is the same word on either sign. judge.rs names both\nletter-writing dialects.\n\nPinned by fourth_axis_pose::{the_doosan_dialect_refuses_a_b_on_its_a_only_table,\nthe_doosan_dialect_refuses_a_turning_a_stated_along_minus_x,\nan_upright_a0_still_posts_on_a_minus_x_fanuc_table}.\n\nRefs #797\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
